1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called…

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Come on! You can’t be serious!

14
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
[laughing]

15
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Oh, I am quite serious.

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The winners will pass the Exam
and earn the title of Hunter.

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
CAN'T WIN x BUT x CAN'T LOSE

18
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
[narrator] The nine remaining applicants,

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Gon,

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Killua,

21
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Kurapika,

22
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Leorio,

23
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Pokkle, Bodoro,

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Gittarackur,

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Hanzo

26
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
and Hisoka,

27
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
having passed the Fourth Phase,

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
head to the site
of the Final Phase of the Exam.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Netero] Well, gentlemen.

30
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Everyone rested up?
Good.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Now then. The Hunter Exam Committee
runs this hotel.

32
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
So, I want all of you
to make yourselves at home

33
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
until the battles have concluded.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
For the Final Phase of the Hunter Exam

35
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
you’ll be competing
in a one-on-one tournament.

36
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
[Leorio] Hold on a second.

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
So only the last person standing passes?

38
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Netero] No.

39
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
You only need one win to pass this phase.

40
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Just one?

41
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Wait. So, in this tournament…

42
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
See, it’s the winners who will drop away

43
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
and the losers
who will advance to the next round.

44
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Which means

45
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
the person who finishes at the top
will not pass.

46
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Make sense to everyone?

47
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
You’re saying that only one person
will fail the Exam.

48
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Exactly.

49
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Here is the bracket we’ve put together.

50
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Impressive, yes?

51
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
You see under this format

52
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
every competitor has at least two chances
to win a round.

53
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Yeah but some people
get five chances to win,

54
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
like Numbers 294 and 405.

55
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Couldn’t you have used
a more balanced bracket?

56
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
[thoughtful grunt]
Now, that’s a fair question.

57
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
This bracket was carefully assembled

58
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
based on each
of your individual performances

59
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
throughout the Hunter Exam.

60
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
To put it simply,

61
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
those whose performances
were rated highly,

62
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
will have the most chances to win.

63
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[Killua] I’m not convinced.

64
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Could you explain exactly
how you scored our performances?

65
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Hmm...

66
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[yells] No!

67
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[Killua] Why not?

68
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
[Netero laughs]

69
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
I can’t say because your scores
are classified.

70
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
I can’t reveal your actual scores.

71
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
However, I can explain
the criteria we used.

72
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
We start with the basics.

73
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
There are three categories.

74
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
There’s physical strength,

75
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
mental acuity

76
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
and lastly, overall impression.

77
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
When judging physical strength, we rely on

78
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
an aggregate of agility, flexibility,
endurance,

79
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
and perception.

80
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
For mental acuity the aggregate
consists of

81
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
resilience, adaptability, judgment,

82
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
and of course, creativity.

83
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
But these are only reference points.

84
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
After all, every last one of you
was strong enough in mind and body

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
to reach the Final Phase.

86
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
We’re most concerned
with your overall impression.

87
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
This refers to any intangible factors

88
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
that defy basic categorization.

89
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
[chuckles]

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Think of it as our way
of assessing your potential as a Hunter.

91
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
We round out our assessment by
incorporating the opinions of your peers.

92
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,000
There you have it.

93
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
[Killua] Based on my performance,
I should be ranked higher.

94
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Do I have less potential than Gon?

95
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
The rules of the battle
are really quite simple.

96
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Weapons are allowed,
cheating is forbidden,

97
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
and if your opponent admits defeat,
you win.

98
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,000
However!

99
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
If you kill your opponent,

100
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
you will be disqualified
without hesitation.

101
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
And if that happens, the Exam ends

102
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
and the remaining applicants pass.

103
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Got it?

104
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
[Masta]
Let the Final Phase of the Exam begin!

105
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
[Hanzo cracking his wrists]

106
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,000
The first match:

107
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Hanzo versus Gon.

108
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Enter!

109
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[trumpets playing fanfare]

110
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
I’m Masta.

111
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
I’ll be serving as referee
for the tournament.

112
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Good luck. Both of you.

113
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Hey. Good to see you again.

114
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
You were the one who was tailing me around
during the Fourth Phase.

115
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
You noticed that, did you?

116
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Naturally.

117
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:36,000
I assume that each of the Examiners
was assigned an Examinee to follow.

118
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Well, I’m sure I wasn’t the only one
who noticed.

119
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
I had no idea!

120
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Oh, I definitely noticed.

121
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
I noticed, but didn’t think
it was worth mentioning.

122
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Uh. Yeah…

123
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
How was I supposed to know?

124
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
I’m very grateful.

125
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,000
You recognized my talent
and my rank improved as a result.

126
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
But no surprise there, really.

127
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Sure, but...

128
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[Hanzo] Now, moving on.

129
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
I have a question for you.

130
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
What is it?

131
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
[Hanzo] We can only win
if our opponent surrenders.

132
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Correct?

133
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
[Hanzo]
Knocking them unconscious doesn’t count.

134
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
No TKOs either?

135
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Right. Those are the rules.

136
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Hmm...

137
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
I see.

138
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Well. This one might prove difficult.

139
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
He looks tough.

140
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
but we should be pretty even
in strength and speed.

141
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
I’ve just gotta keep him on the move
‘til I see an opening.

142
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Now, time to start.

143
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
All right, Gon. Get him!

144
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
I wonder how he’ll do against Hanzo.

145
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Begin!

146
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
I’ll keep some distance.

147
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[gasps]

148
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
You must think you’re
pretty quick on your feet, don’t you?

149
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,000
I’ll give you that.

150
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[choking sounds]

151
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Not half bad for a little kid.

152
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[scoffs]

153
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
I could have dodged that no problem.

154
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
[choking sounds]

155
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Now if this were a regular match,

156
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
I’d already be declared the winner.

157
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
C’mon, pull yourself together.

158
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
-[bones crackling]
-[Gon grunts]

159
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
You must feel awful.

160
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
I hit you hard enough
to bounce your brain around your skull.

161
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
You get it? You don’t stand a chance.

162
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Just give up
and spare yourself the trouble.

163
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
[straining]

164
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
No way!

165
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
-[Gon coughing]
-Think hard about it.

166
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Surrender now
and you’ll have another chance.

167
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
But being stubborn
isn’t gonna get you anywhere.

168
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
So just give up.

169
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
That’s never gonna happen!

170
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[groans]

171
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
-[Gon groans weakly]
-Say it.

172
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
[Gon groans]

173
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[Gon groans in pain]

174
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Gon! Don’t push it!

175
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
You still have other fights!

176
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
-So just--
-[Kurapika] Leorio!

177
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
If you were in Gon’s position,
would you give up?

178
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Hell, no, I wouldn’t!

179
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
He thinks he’s so tough…

180
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
[Kurapika] Gon feels the same.

181
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Come on! I know that!

182
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,000
But it doesn’t look like
he has much of a choice!

183
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
My point exactly.
But I understand.

184
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
-[Gon grunts]
-[Kurapika and Leorio wince]

185
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
[grunts]

186
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Surrender, Gon! This is suicide!

187
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
[Menchi] This is unbelievable.

188
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
The Chairman’s mean streak
is really in a class by itself!

189
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Wait, what do you mean?

190
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
No applicant who’s made it
all the way to here,

191
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
is going to simply give up a fight
that easily.

192
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[Buhara] That’s true.

193
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
-[Gon groans]
-This fight isn’t just peculiar.

194
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
A system like this is completely crazy.

195
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
The kid’s in real danger.

196
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[groaning quietly in pain]

197
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

198
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[Leorio smirks]

199
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
HANZO

200
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[blows]

201
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[thud]

202
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Leorio growling quietly]

203
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Three whole hours? Damn.

204
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Look. He can’t even vomit anymore.

205
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Now get up.

206
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
[Leorio growls] Enough already!

207
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
I’m gonna kill you, hear me?

208
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Pick on someone your own size!

209
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
If you can’t handle it,
you’d better leave.

210
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
It’s only going to get worse.

211
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
What the hell did you say?

212
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
There’ll be no interference
in a one-on-one match.

213
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Stay back.

214
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
If you try to help him in any way,

215
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Gon will be instantly disqualified!

216
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[Gon] It’s okay.

217
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Leorio…

218
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
This is...

219
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
this is nothing.

220
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Really.

221
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[growls quietly]

222
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
I can still fight him.

223
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
[frustrated growl]

224
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
[Gon grunts]

225
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
-I’ll break your arm.
-[Gon gasps]

226
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[groaning quietly]

227
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
I’m not kidding.

228
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Now say it.

229
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Say you surrender.

230
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
-[yells] Never!
-[thud]

231
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[Gon groaning quietly]

232
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[groans in pain]

233
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
He actually broke it.

234
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
[Hanzo] There.

235
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Now you won’t be able
to use your left arm anymore.

236
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
[grinding teeth in frustration]

237
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Leorio] Don’t try to stop me, Kurapika.

238
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:03,000
If that bastard does anything else,
Gon will fail the exam.

239
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
'Cause I won’t be able to stop myself.

240
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
[Kurapika] Me?

241
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
You think I’ll stop you?

242
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Don’t worry.

243
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
There’s no chance of that.

244
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
[Hanzo] I’m sure you’re in too much pain
to listen,

245
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
but hear this.

246
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:25,000
I’m a descendant of a clandestine group
called the shinobi.

247
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
From the day I was born,

248
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
I’ve been subjected
to intensive training

249
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:36,000
in order to master
the special art of ninpo.

250
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
For the past 18 years

251
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,000
I’ve tirelessly trained my body
and honed my technique.

252
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,000
By the time I was your age,
I had already killed.

253
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[scoffs] Not like it’s that big a deal.

254
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[Hanzo] At this point in time

255
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
you have no hope
of defeating me in combat.

256
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
I’m being nice.

257
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
So just admit defeat--

258
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[grunts in pain]

259
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[Gon groans in pain]

260
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Dammit!

261
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Between the pain and you blabbing

262
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
I don’t know what cleared my head up more!

263
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Hell yeah!

264
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Atta boy!

265
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Now kick him while he’s down
and he’s finished!

266
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
If you’re eighteen,

267
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
then you’re just six years older than me.

268
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Besides this isn’t a battle
to see who’s stronger.

269
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
It’s to see who’s willing
to throw in the towel first.

270
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
I let you kick me because I wanted to.

271
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
You’re a liar!

272
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[Hanzo] You must be confused.

273
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
That was not a warning.

274
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
It was a direct order.

275
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Was it too hard for you to understand?

276
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
I’m quite happy to break it down for you.

277
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
I’ll cut off your legs,

278
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
so that they can’t be reattached.

279
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
A permanent injury

280
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
should open up your eyes
to the current situation.

281
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
But before we must resort to such things,

282
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
I want to hear you surrender.

283
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
[Gon] Well, that’s a problem.

284
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
I don’t want to have my legs cut off

285
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,000
but I don’t want to surrender, either.

286
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
How ‘bout we find
a different way to fight?

287
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[yells] What the hell?

288
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Have you not been paying attention?

289
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
-[Hisoka chuckling]
-[Bodoro laughing]

290
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Oh, pardon me.

291
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Are you really making demands?
You messin’ with me?

292
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
I’m seriously about to cut your legs off!

293
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
You do what you want but I won’t give up!

294
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[growling in anger]

295
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Besides if you cut my legs off,

296
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
I’ll probably just bleed to death.

297
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,000
[Hanzo] What?

298
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Mister Masta?
He’d be disqualified for that, right?

299
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Uh... Yes.

300
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:06,000
See?

301
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
And that’d be bad for the both of us.

302
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
So, let’s think of a better way.

303
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
[angered growling]

304
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[growling loudly]

305
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[Kurapika chuckles] I think Gon is okay.

306
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
He’s in control now.

307
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
He’s just so damn stubborn!

308
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
But he’s also convincing
to Hanzo and the rest of us.

309
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Impressive.

310
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
[Killua] What the hell is this?

311
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Nothing’s changed.

312
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
I mean, it’s not like
Gon’s gotten any stronger.

313
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
His arm is still broken and everything!

314
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
But what happened to the mood in here?

315
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
It was so tense a second ago.

316
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Why did it get so much lighter?

317
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
[angered growling]

318
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
[Hanzo] I see you’re not getting it,
so I’ll try again.

319
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Die and you’ll never get another chance.

320
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
If I kill you right here and now,

321
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
I only need to come back
and take the Exam again next year.

322
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
We are not on equal footing!

323
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[Killua] He’s right, Gon.

324
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
You might have the edge
when it comes to brains

325
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
but you don’t have the combat skills
he does.

326
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
That’s not something
you can make up for right now.

327
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
In the end, it all comes down to ability.

328
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[Leorio grunts]

329
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[grunting]

330
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
What’s wrong?

331
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
It’s just a stupid sentence!

332
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Think! Give up
and you can still try again next year!

333
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Is your pride truly
all that you care about?

334
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Even more than your life?
Is it worth dying for?

335
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[grunts]

336
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
I’m gonna go see my dad.

337
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Your dad?

338
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
See, my dad is a Hunter.

339
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
So, I’m gonna become a Hunter
exactly like he is

340
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
and then I’ll be able to meet him!

341
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
I know I’ll find him someday.

342
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:37,000
But... I feel like if I surrender now,

343
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
I’m never gonna find him!

344
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,000
So, I won’t give up.

345
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Surrender...

346
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
or you will die.

347
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
So, logic had nothing to do with it.

348
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Fine. You win.

349
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,000
I give up, okay?

350
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
I’m not allowed to kill you.

351
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:18,000
And I just can’t think of another way
to force you to surrender.

352
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
So, I’ll take my chances
in the next round.

353
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Well, I can’t accept that.

354
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
No fair!

355
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
We both have to come up with some way
that we can have a proper match!

356
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,000
[Hanzo sighs]

357
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Why am I not surprised?

358
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
[yells]
You just said you would never surrender,

359
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
so what the hell is the point of that,
you idiot?

360
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
The point is that I don’t want
to win like this, okay?

361
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Then what do you suggest?

362
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Let’s work together and figure it out!

363
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
So, in other words...

364
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
I’ve already given up the match

365
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:56,000
but you want me to continue fighting
and try to beat you again right?

366
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:59,000
But first we have to work together
to find a way you can win,

367
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
so you feel good about your victory.

368
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Is that right?

369
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Yeah!

370
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[yells] Moron!

371
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Hey, referee.

372
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
I lose, so move on to the next match.

373
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Understood, sir.

374
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
But I’d like to say something first.

375
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Whenever he wakes up,

376
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
he’ll probably decline his advancement.

377
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
And as we’ve all seen,
he can be incredibly stubborn.

378
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Only one person fails this round, right?

379
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
So, if Gon is disqualified,

380
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
wouldn’t that render
the rest of our upcoming fights

381
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
completely meaningless?

382
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
[narrator] With Hanzo’s concession,
Gon’s victory has been assured.

383
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,000
The Final Phase

384
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:50,000
that will determine
the single failing applicant

385
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,000
has only just begun.

386
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,000
[theme song playing]

387
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Baffling Turn x Of x Events!"

388
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon gibers]

389
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Killua]
They stuck a needle in Gon, too?
